WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.839
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:08.723
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.023 --> 00:00:14.996
Unit sixteen: Writing a Review. Today you will write a review of a book, film or place.

4
00:00:15.296 --> 00:00:17.821
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:21.907
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:23.705
Review.

7
00:00:24.717 --> 00:00:27.204
Review means a report that gives an opinion.

8
00:00:27.817 --> 00:00:29.352
Write a review of the film.

9
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.776
Your turn. Say: Review.

10
00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:36.414
Review.

11
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:37.965
Plot.

12
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.019
Plot means the main events of a story.

13
00:00:41.617 --> 00:00:43.024
The plot is simple.

14
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:45.944
Your turn. Say: Plot.

15
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:49.476
Plot.

16
00:00:50.217 --> 00:00:51.253
Recommend.

17
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.609
Recommend means to say something is good.

18
00:00:55.217 --> 00:00:56.694
I recommend this book.

19
00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:59.843
Your turn. Say: Recommend.

20
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.794
Recommend.

21
00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:05.214
Rating.

22
00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:08.715
Rating means a score that shows quality.

23
00:01:09.317 --> 00:01:11.409
It has a rating of four stars.

24
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:14.100
Your turn. Say: Rating.

25
00:01:16.967 --> 00:01:17.747
Rating.

26
00:01:18.483 --> 00:01:19.705
Entertaining.

27
00:01:20.717 --> 00:01:23.157
Entertaining means enjoyable and fun.

28
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.297
The show was entertaining.

29
00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:28.454
Your turn. Say: Entertaining.

30
00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.406
Entertaining.

31
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.325
Disappointing.

32
00:01:35.317 --> 00:01:37.630
Disappointing means not as good as hoped.

33
00:01:38.217 --> 00:01:39.787
The ending was disappointing.

34
00:01:40.383 --> 00:01:42.966
Your turn. Say: Disappointing.

35
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.149
Disappointing.

36
00:01:47.883 --> 00:01:48.861
Overall.

37
00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:52.291
Overall means considering everything.

38
00:01:52.883 --> 00:01:54.976
Overall, it is a fine film.

39
00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:58.294
Your turn. Say: Overall.

40
00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.367
Overall.

41
00:02:03.117 --> 00:02:03.920
Worth.

42
00:02:04.917 --> 00:02:07.392
Worth means good enough for the price or time.

43
00:02:07.983 --> 00:02:09.333
It is worth watching.

44
00:02:09.917 --> 00:02:12.174
Your turn. Say: Worth.

45
00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:15.895
Worth.

46
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.525
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:23.429
Visal, what is in a good review?

48
00:02:24.517 --> 00:02:32.916
Say what the film or book is about without telling the ending. Then give your opinion with reasons and finish with a recommendation.

49
00:02:34.017 --> 00:02:35.621
Which adjectives help?

50
00:02:36.717 --> 00:02:45.638
Use specific adjectives such as entertaining, moving, slow or disappointing. Avoid only saying good or bad.

51
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.902
How do I end?

52
00:02:49.017 --> 00:02:54.885
Say who will enjoy it. For example, I recommend it to anyone who likes adventure.

53
00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:57.917
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:58.783 --> 00:03:01.131
Grammar focus: Recommending.

55
00:03:01.431 --> 00:03:02.548
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.737
I recommend it to anyone who likes adventure.

57
00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.044
I would recommend this book to every student.

58
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.719
End a review with I recommend plus who will enjoy it. Do not tell the ending of the story.

59
00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:18.937
Be careful! Don't say: I recommend to you it.

60
00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.109
Say: I recommend it to you.

61
00:03:23.409 --> 00:03:24.770
Put the object first.

62
00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:28.231
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.325
A Film Review.

64
00:03:30.625 --> 00:03:33.263
Kunthea reviews a film about a young fisherman.

65
00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:36.069
The plot is simple but moving.

66
00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:39.879
The acting is excellent and the music is beautiful.

67
00:03:40.867 --> 00:03:42.622
The ending is a little slow.

68
00:03:43.633 --> 00:03:46.759
Overall, she gives it four stars and recommends it.

69
00:03:47.867 --> 00:03:51.810
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.278
A review gives an blank.

71
00:03:54.578 --> 00:03:57.767
A, address. B, opinion. C, order.

72
00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:02.996
The answer is B: opinion.

73
00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.778
The plot is the main blank.

74
00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:09.755
A, actor. B, price. C, events.

75
00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:15.265
The answer is C: events.

76
00:04:16.417 --> 00:04:17.871
Do not tell the blank.

77
00:04:18.171 --> 00:04:21.325
A, ending. B, title. C, name.

78
00:04:24.867 --> 00:04:26.495
The answer is A: ending.

79
00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.162
A rating shows blank.

80
00:04:29.462 --> 00:04:32.779
A, colour. B, quality. C, size.

81
00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:38.333
The answer is B: quality.

82
00:04:39.483 --> 00:04:41.320
Kunthea gives it four blank.

83
00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.925
A, hats. B, cats. C, stars.

84
00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.826
The answer is C: stars.

85
00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:55.138
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:04:55.983 --> 00:04:57.414
How do you write a review?

87
00:05:06.217 --> 00:05:07.647
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:07.947 --> 00:05:19.356
I say what the film or book is about without giving the ending. I give my opinion with reasons and specific adjectives. I finish with a recommendation and a rating.

89
00:05:19.656 --> 00:05:21.656
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:26.224
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and recommending.

91
00:05:26.524 --> 00:05:32.566
Today's value is authenticity. Lead as your true self, guided by your real values.

92
00:05:32.866 --> 00:05:35.588
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:35.888 --> 00:05:39.086
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

